    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP\u2019s May 13th slate, our primary focus is capitalizing on speed and favorable matchups against soft pitching rotations. **Corbin Carroll** (81.94) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) headline our lineup today. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a plus-matchup against Kumar Rocker, where his speed profile is further amplified by the pitcher's slow delivery, creating a high-ceiling environment for stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime spot against Mitch Keller; the combination of a strong wind-out forecast and a massive +14% boost from a favorable platoon advantage makes him an elite play despite being lower in the batting order. **Josh Naylor** (74.98) also rounds out the top-tier, fueled by a high-skill matchup against a struggling Lance McCullers Jr.\n\nStrategic lineup construction heavily influenced our roster decisions, particularly regarding the fringe spots. **James Wood** (69.37) remains a mandatory start due to his high xwOBA and wind-aided park factors, effectively neutralizing the threat of Nick Lodolo. In contrast, **Kyle Karros** (49.64) was our most difficult benching decision. While his park factors and recent performance metrics were solid, he ultimately fell short of our efficiency floor due to a lack of platoon leverage compared to **Vinnie Pasquantino** or **Tyler Soderstrom**. Investors should remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**; should either fall out of their assumed spots, their efficiency scores will drift toward the marginal range. Furthermore, **Brice Turang** faces a tricky outing against Michael King; while he benefits from a leadoff position, we are factoring in a 4% efficiency penalty due to King's ability to control the running game, which slightly hampers **Brice Turang**'s primary value proposition.",
